A template is expanded during the check into String concatenation: it is a String like any other. With only
constant holes it is folded to a constant; a hole that calls a Runtime native runs at runtime.
$[Import* std]
$[# who "Ada"]
$[# greeting f"{Hi $who}"]
$[% greeting] ${= greeting "Hi Ada"} $[% f"{x ${+ 1 2}}"]
expect: "Hi Ada"
expect: true
expect: "x 3"
$f"{now ${time}}"
input: std.time=5
expect: "now 5"
